## Modules: Oview.sys
## Inspired by Gnome Activity overview and Taviso’s WindowList function – FvwmExpose
## https://zensites.net/fvwm/guide/advanced_functions.html

SetEnv HOME_DIR $[HOME]/.fvwm
SetEnv CORE_DIR $[HOME]/.fvwm/core

SetEnv wo-icon $[CORE_DIR]/7Modules/FvwmOverView/icons

Module FvwmButtons FvwmOverView

DestroyModuleConfig FvwmOverView: *
*FvwmOverView: Geometry 77x36+10+50
*FvwmOverView: PressColorset 32
*FvwmOverView: Frame 0
*FvwmOverView: Rows 1
*FvwmOverView: Columns 1
*FvwmOverView: Padding 0 0

*FvwmOverView: (46x1, Colorset 62, Icon $[wo-icon]/appsView-38x38.png, Action(Mouse 1) 'Read $[CORE_DIR]/7Modules/FvwmOverView/OverView/WinListExpose.sys')

## Style setting
Style FvwmOverView !Borders, !Title, WindowListSkip, StaysOnTop, Sticky, NeverFocus

## Key binding
## Use FvwmCoomand as a short delay so X11 handles the window
## capture properly. Add FvwmMFL.
#

Module FvwmMFL

DestroyFunc FoverView
AddToFunc FoverView
+ I Read $[CORE_DIR]/7Modules/FvwmOverView/OverView/WinListExpose.sys

# (ctrl-w)
Silent Key w A C PipeRead "FvwmCommand FoverView"

## Top window focus.
## This function is for "Style * ClickToFocus" users.
## Check ....OverView/WinListExpose.sys
